    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A kingdom of south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> that grew from one of sixteen rival realms into the dominant power of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</li><li>Its kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bimbisara">Bimbisara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajatashatru">Ajatashatru</a> were patrons of the Buddha and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahavira">Mahavira</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajgir">Rajagriha</a> hosted the First Buddhist Council.</li><li>Its conquests and its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pataliputra">Pataliputra</a> became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanda-dynasty">Nanda</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya</a> and later Gupta empires.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Buddhist texts say <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bimbisara">Bimbisara</a> once summoned the headmen of the 80,000 villages of his kingdom to an assembly, then sent them to see the Buddha.</p></aside>
    </section>

